@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Page layout)

Columns, boxes, spacing, page breaks, headers, footers and fixed pages.

@section(Alignment and spacing)

@subsection(@@align)

Aligns everything inside it: left, right, center or justify.

@align(center)
All of this is centred.
@end

@align(justify)
A justified paragraph.
@end

@subsection(@@hspace)

A horizontal gap of a given length.

@hspace(2em)

@subsection(@@vspace)

A vertical gap of a given length.

@vspace(2em)

@vspace(1cm)

@subsection(@@hfill)

A flexible horizontal spacer — pushes what follows to the right.

@hfill

@subsection(@@vfill)

A flexible vertical spacer — pushes what follows to the bottom.

@vfill

@subsection(@@centertext)

Template-layer centred text, optionally placed absolutely — used by generated layouts and stylesheets.

@centertext(text=Final Exam)

@centertext(text=Name, x=2in, y=1in, w=4in)
@col

@section(Columns)

@subsection(@@columns)

Columns side by side, split by col — or, with flow, text that runs from one column into the next and ends level (balanced) on screen and in the PDF.

@columns(count=2)
left text
@col
right text
@end

@columns(3, flow)
…text that flows…
@end

@columns(2, flow, gap=1.5em)
…
@end

@subsection(@@cols)

Auto-flowing columns; col splits them.

@cols(count=2)
left text
@col
right text
@end

@subsection(@@col)

The column break inside columns — and the column split on a two-column slide.

@subsection(@@colbreak)

What follows starts the next column of a two-column paper or a columns(n, flow) block.

@colbreak

@subsection(@@multicol)

Auto-flowing item columns: mark each item with item (or next) — or mark nothing and every source line is an item — and the column count falls out of the width, on screen and in print.

@multicol(min=170)
@item one
@item two
@item three
@end

@multicol(cols=3, header=1)
Section A
q1
q2
@end

@subsection(@@next)

The item marker inside multicol — identical to item, both spellings read naturally.

@subsection(@@wide)

Content across both columns of a two-column paper (LaTeX's figure* or widetext).

@wide
@table(sep=|)
…
@endtable
@end

@wide(at=bottom)
…
@end

@section(Boxes)

@subsection(@@box)

An absolutely-placed box: position it with x/y, size it with w/h, style it with bg/border/pad.

@box(x=2cm, y=3cm, w=6cm)
content
@end

@box(w=40%, bg=#eef, pad=8px, align=center) … @end

@box(w=40%, style=qrbox)
…
@end

@box(x=1in, y=1in, w=3in) …@end
@endpage

@box(w=40%, h=3cm, color=#1e3a8a, border=1px solid #93c5fd, fs=10pt, radius=8pt, shadow, title=A titled box, titlebg=#dbeafe)
A box with a height, text colour, border, font size, rounded corners, a shadow and a title band.
@end

@box(w=30%, float=right, rounded, bg=#f0fdf4)
Floats to the right; text wraps beside it.
@end
The text that follows a floating box runs beside it until the box ends. This sentence is here to show the wrap.

@box(w=30%, float=left, align=left)
Floats left, text aligned left.
@end
More running text beside the left box.

@box(w=30%, align=right)
Aligned right.
@end

@box(w=4cm, h=4cm, shape=circle, bg=#fef3c7, align=center)
A circle
@end

Stacking order on a fixed page, back to front:
@page(w=12cm, h=4cm)
@box(x=0.5cm, y=0.5cm, w=5cm, h=3cm, bg=#e0e7ff, z=back)
z=back
@end
@box(x=2cm, y=1cm, w=5cm, h=2.5cm, bg=#fde68a, z=behind)
z=behind
@end
@box(x=4cm, y=1.5cm, w=5cm, h=2cm, bg=#fecaca, z=front)
z=front
@end
@endpage

@box(w=50%, theme=tip)
theme= names a box style, the same as style=.
@end

@subsection(@@boxstyle)

How a box looks, by name — boxstyle(qrbox, bg=#eef2ff, border=1pt solid #1d4ed8, radius=6pt, pad=8pt); then box(x=…, y=…, style=qrbox) says only where the box goes.

@boxstyle(qrbox, bg=#eef2ff, border=1pt solid #1d4ed8, radius=6pt, pad=8pt)

@boxstyle(card, w=60%, bg=#f8fafc, border=1pt solid #cbd5e1, color=#0f172a, shadow, title=Card)

@boxstyle(warncard, extends=card, bg=#fff7ed, title=Warning)

@box(style=card)
A box drawn from the card style.
@end

@box(style=warncard)
The same card, extended with another colour and title.
@end

@subsection(@@rotate)

A table or figure turned a quarter (90 clockwise, -90 anticlockwise) or 180 degrees, taking its turned size on the page — a wide table set sideways.

@rotate(90)
@table(sep=|)
…
@endtable
@end

@rotate(-90)
…
@end

@section(Pages)

@subsection(@@pagesetup)

Paper size and margins for the whole document (put it in a .style to share it): landscape; binding margins inner= / outer= (twoside mirrors them on even pages); the page-number style pagenumbers=1 \| i \| I \| a \| A \| Page 1 of N \| off.

@pagesetup(size=letter, margin=1in)

@pagesetup(size=a4, margin=2cm)

@pagesetup(landscape)

@pagesetup(inner=1.5in, outer=1in, twoside)

@pagesetup(pagenumbers=i)

@subsection(@@header)

A running page header with left / center / right slots.

@header(left=Course, center=Exam 1, right=Page)

@header(left={section}, right=Page {page} of {pages}, first=none)

@header(left={title}, right={page}, even=mirror)

@subsection(@@footer)

A running page footer with left / center / right slots — the same tokens and first= / even= as header.

@footer(center={page})

@footer(left={title}, right=Page {page} of {pages})

@subsection(@@newpage)

A page break.

@newpage

@newpage(odd)

@newpage(odd, numbers=1)

@newpage(numbers=Page 1 of N)
@next

@subsection(@@watermark)

Big faded text behind the page content (DRAFT, CONFIDENTIAL…).

@watermark(DRAFT)

@watermark(text=CONFIDENTIAL, opacity=0.08)

@subsection(@@page)

A fixed-geometry page: everything inside is positioned in real page coordinates.

@page(w=8.5in, h=2in)
@box(x=1in, y=0.4in, w=4in)
Placed one inch from the left edge of a fixed page.
@end
@endpage

@@fixedpage is the same as @@page:
@fixedpage(w=8.5in, h=1in)
@box(x=1in, y=0.2in, w=3in)
On a fixed page.
@end
@endpage

@subsection(@@pack)

A shared document's tail — every stylesheet, include, picture and data file the document needs, appended as ONE block so the file opens the same on any machine.

@pack(v=1, mode=edit, sha=0000)
manifest
{"root":"quiz3.idoc","entries":[]}
@end
